  "gaps": [
    "The capture states 'credit hours' but does not explicitly say whether these are semester or quarter hours; semester was assumed and should be verified.",
    "Major requirements total 41 credit hours, but the listed foundation courses (22) plus Groups A, B and C (12) account for only 34; the source of the remaining 7 major credits is not stated (possibly from 'Additional Course Offerings' PY 399, PY 445, PY 450 or other upper-level psychology courses).",
    "The role of 'Additional Course Offerings' (PY 399 Topics in Psychology, 3 credits; PY 445 and PY 450, 1-6 credits each) in meeting the major is not stated.",
    "MA 102 College Algebra 'can be completed as part of the General Education requirements'; whether its 3 credits count within the 37 general education credits (to avoid double counting) is not confirmed.",
    "Required laboratory science course ('One laboratory science course (Biology or Chemistry preferred, but not required)') has no credit amount or course code printed; it may also count toward general education.",
    "Kirkpatrick Signature Series requirement: courses, credits, and whether it falls within general education are not stated on this page.",
    "Specific general education course/cluster requirements within the 37 credits are not listed in the capture.",
    "No residency (credits that must be completed at Bellevue University) or transfer-credit limits are stated in the capture.",
    "Catalog year is not stated; current students are directed to BRUIN 'Academic Progress' for official curriculum requirements."
  ],
